    "result_text": "The full suite passes (2 tests, both green; the other files are the abstract base and a support helper). \n\nThe change is complete:\n\n- **`DuplicateTelephoneException`** \u2014 a new runtime exception thrown on create when a normalized telephone is already taken.\n- **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 a new `@ExceptionHandler` mapping that exception to **409 Conflict**, with an `errors: [\"telephone\"]` body consistent with the existing telephone/validation handlers.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the telephone (existing 10-digit normalization), it now calls `rejectDuplicateTelephone(...)`, which scans existing owners and throws if any already uses that normalized value. Since telephones are always normalized on create, a plain equality comparison against stored values is exact.\n\nBoth the new duplicate-rejection test (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` \u2192 409) and the distinct-telephone test pass, and nothing else regressed.",
